      "Each own manual establishes the distinct PCLK configuration domain, APBEN2.AWT configuration gate, active-low APBRST2.AWT reset, IRQ30, Timer=3, PRS1..15, EN/ARR sequence and UD R1W0 with no-op seed63.",
      "The manuals do not describe an LSE-edge acknowledgment for these local AWT accesses. Local control after counting-source loss is a bounded inference requiring working CPU/PCLK/gate/reset, not a measured silicon timing guarantee.",
      "L031/R031/W031 FILTER7 consumes standalone AWT underflow. Classic FILTER7 is not qualified. Existing GPIOC acquisition/reacquisition can advance retained filters/edges; health observations do not add a bank scan.",
      "Readiness, retained UD, CNT samples and elapsed wall time remain distinct. Loss supplies no guaranteed AWT wake, fallback or continued event, and waits can remain pending indefinitely.",
      "Classic required-write-one CCS tables govern current HAL admission while their narratives retain software enable prerequisites; this is not a hardware-fixed detector claim."
    ]
